    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="88d82b9a-0d37-52a6-994b-74d41b551009" activityNameId="511a1ace-2ac5-571a-a9ae-50087ff9bb0b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, dust, unalloyed EAF steel, 15.4% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, dust, unalloyed EAF steel, 15.4% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% dust from unalloyed electric steel production to landfill; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O 105410; O 75250; H n.a.; C 11979; S 7187.1; N n.a.; P 1672.9; B n.a.; Cl 26353; Br n.a.; F 4408.1; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As 397.69; Ba n.a.; Cd 574.97; Co 14.374; Cr 3934; Cu 2635.3; Hg 5.2705; Mn 29686; Mo n.a.; Ni 287.48; Pb 32582; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V 335.4; Zn 215610; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 14558; Fe 359360; Ca 65063; Al 2535.9; K 10739; Mg 17337; Na 12086; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 0%. ;; UUID: d1ca3d5f-519a-4577-9579-e94dd5e964c6
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. 
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d1ca3d5f-519a-4577-9579-e94dd5e964c6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
